For the boundary layer on \( y = 0 \) in a converging channel, the mainstream velocity is \( U(x) = - rac{Q}{x} \). The boundary layer equation (8.26) is: \[ u  rac{\partial u}{\partial x} + v  rac{\partial u}{\partial y} = -  rac{Q^{2}}{x^{3}} + 
u  rac{\partial^{2} u}{\partial y^{2}}. \] Assuming a similarity solution: \[ u = - rac{Q}{x} f'(\eta), \quad \eta =  rac{y}{
u^{ rac{1}{2}} x / |Q|^{ rac{1}{2}}}, \] the stream function \( \psi = -
u^{ rac{1}{2}} |Q|^{ rac{1}{2}} f(\eta) \) gives: \[ v = - rac{\partial \psi}{\partial x} = - rac{|Q|^{ rac{1}{2}} 
u^{ rac{1}{2}}}{x} \eta f'. \] Substituting into eqn (8.26) and simplifying yields: \[ f'^{2} = 1 + f''. \] Defining \( F(\eta) = f'(\eta) \), we obtain: \[ F'' + 1 - F^{2} = 0, \] with boundary conditions \( F(0) = 0 \) (no-slip) and \( F(\infty) = 1 \) (matching the mainstream).

